This seems a little bit too complicated. Like, I'm not sure that the problem as you state it is really a problem. If you are a proper noun that is also a personal name, it will almost always be said in the way that the common noun is (this is true of all you list except maybe bolivar but i'm willing to take that loss -- and ones like it, I think -- for the simplicity). I think we can just replace almost all of this with a rule that wikipedia labels it as a common noun, then we just cull it out. 

